WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.851
My name is Elizabeth Willard, and I am a 22-year-old teacher.

2
00:00:04.852 --> 00:00:12.862
I graduated from the Hartford Female Seminary in Connecticut, one of the first schools in America that trains female teachers.

3
00:00:12.863 --> 00:00:21.377
In 1854 I began teaching in the new territory of Kansas, an area located in the middle of the United States.

4
00:00:21.378 --> 00:00:27.286
There are many teaching jobs in the West because many whites have been settling here from the East.

5
00:00:27.287 --> 00:00:30.838
New frontier towns have popped up everywhere.

6
00:00:30.839 --> 00:00:38.034
My teacher training started when I was twenty, and I learned spelling, mathematics, and music.

7
00:00:38.035 --> 00:00:44.937
Before graduation my classmates and I were invited to teach out West when we completed our studies.

8
00:00:44.938 --> 00:00:49.955
Some teaching students accepted the offer, and I was one of them.

9
00:00:49.956 --> 00:00:55.617
We trained for frontier life by carrying pails of water and chopping firewood.

10
00:00:55.618 --> 00:01:00.270
We needed to be tough to face the many hardships ahead.

11
00:01:00.271 --> 00:01:07.375
When we graduated, a school committee gave us our teaching posts, and I was assigned to a school in Kansas.

12
00:01:07.376 --> 00:01:15.646
All the teachers traveled west in the spring, and since it was unsafe for women to travel alone, my father went with me.

13
00:01:15.647 --> 00:01:24.677
First, we rode on horseback for two weeks, about eight hundred kilometers, from Hartford, Connecticut, to Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania.

14
00:01:24.678 --> 00:01:31.598
Then, we took a steamboat down the Ohio River from Pittsburgh through the states of Ohio and Kentucky.

15
00:01:31.599 --> 00:01:39.509
After 12 days we arrived in Old Shawneetown, Illinois, and from there I took a stagecoach on my own.

16
00:01:39.510 --> 00:01:48.825
After ten days and another eight hundred kilometers, I arrived at my final destination—Fort Leavenworth, Kansas.

17
00:01:48.826 --> 00:01:57.169
Suddenly I was alone in a strange town, and I had nowhere to stay. So I went to the schoolhouse.

18
00:01:57.170 --> 00:02:04.561
With so few trees for lumber on the prairie, sod and dirt had been used to build the small school, rather than wood.

19
00:02:04.562 --> 00:02:07.553
There was only one room and two windows.

20
00:02:07.554 --> 00:02:12.832
The bathroom was outside, and a little fence wrapped around the schoolyard.

21
00:02:12.833 --> 00:02:16.136
Some of the town's children came by to see me.

22
00:02:16.137 --> 00:02:20.669
One little girl named Abby said I would be staying with her family.

23
00:02:20.670 --> 00:02:26.676
"Boarding around," or staying in students' homes, is common for frontier teachers.

24
00:02:26.677 --> 00:02:32.874
I would have to help Abby's family with the chores, but I was happy to accept their offer.

25
00:02:32.875 --> 00:02:40.978
Boarding helps me save money, since I make only one hundred and fifty dollars a year—half the salary of a male teacher.

26
00:02:40.979 --> 00:02:48.293
Most of my students live on farms, so the school year must fit between the fall harvest and the spring planting.

27
00:02:48.294 --> 00:02:53.865
During my first year, the class size varied from 3 to 25 children.

28
00:02:53.866 --> 00:02:59.696
Some of the children do farm work and other chores and cannot attend every day.

29
00:02:59.697 --> 00:03:03.748
My students' ages range from four to twenty years old.

30
00:03:03.749 --> 00:03:09.936
In my classroom I have a small desk up front, and my students sit on benches in rows.

31
00:03:09.937 --> 00:03:14.480
There is one blackboard, and we have no books except for a Bible.

32
00:03:14.481 --> 00:03:19.345
Sometimes the children bring in old newspapers or magazines from home.

33
00:03:19.346 --> 00:03:25.906
We have no paper supplies, so my students write their lessons on flat rocks called slates.

34
00:03:25.907 --> 00:03:31.014
They write with a soft piece of rock called a slate pen.

35
00:03:31.015 --> 00:03:36.690
Most of my students behave well in class, but sometimes I have to punish them.

36
00:03:36.691 --> 00:03:42.597
If a child talks during a lesson, I put a whispering stick in his or her mouth.

37
00:03:42.598 --> 00:03:49.449
This is a small wooden stick that is held in place by a piece of cloth that I tie around the student's head.

38
00:03:49.450 --> 00:03:54.388
The child is forced to bite on the stick and cannot speak.

39
00:03:54.389 --> 00:04:03.473
Sometimes if a student never knows the correct answer to a question, I put a pointy hat on their head with the word "Dunce" written on it.

40
00:04:03.474 --> 00:04:09.069
When a student wears the dunce cap, it means he or she is not very smart.

41
00:04:09.070 --> 00:04:16.406
My first winter was very hard. The temperature sometimes dropped to -23 degrees Celsius.

42
00:04:16.407 --> 00:04:21.668
The snow started falling in November and did not stop until April.

43
00:04:21.669 --> 00:04:28.081
The only heat we had was a potbellied stove in the classroom, and it was smoky and hard to light.

44
00:04:28.082 --> 00:04:32.359
I'd arrive at school early to chop firewood for the whole day.

45
00:04:32.360 --> 00:04:39.092
Children close to the stove would get too hot. Others, in the back of the room, almost froze.

46
00:04:39.093 --> 00:04:45.690
It was so cold that my students' lunches of dried fruit and salted meat would sometimes freeze.

47
00:04:45.691 --> 00:04:50.796
Some children became sick and died during the year.

48
00:04:50.797 --> 00:04:55.828
We all were happy when spring finally arrived.

49
00:04:55.829 --> 00:05:00.479
I am now at the end of my first year, and I am very lonely.

50
00:05:00.480 --> 00:05:07.491
When I took this job, I promised not to marry for two years, so I could devote myself to my students.

51
00:05:07.492 --> 00:05:11.655
In my free time, I sew quilts and patch my clothes.

52
00:05:11.656 --> 00:05:15.966
I go to church and visit the friends I have met there.

53
00:05:15.967 --> 00:05:21.867
I have heard that some teachers have already gone home because the life out here is too difficult.

54
00:05:21.868 --> 00:05:25.032
But I would like to stay on for another year.

55
00:05:25.033 --> 00:05:32.114
I have grown to love my students and the progress we all have made.

